 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Eleonora threatens to fire Mikhail Jekovich unless he restores order immediately, and sentences Senya and Fedya to work a week without pay and two weeks without days off. Mikhail immediately calls a buyer to get rid of the pony.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "Быстро наведи в отеле порядок!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "Иначе я тебя отсюда вышвырну.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "А вы двое слушайте меня.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "Неделю работаете совсем без зарплаты.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "И две недели без выходных.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "Всё, быстро пошли вон отсюда!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "mikhail",
   "t": "Нет, это я не вам.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "mikhail",
   "t": "Да, я срочно продаю пони.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "mikhail",
   "t": "Ещё как продаю, жду вас.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "Айнура, быстро уберите всё здесь.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "ainura",
   "t": "Я приехала работать в Москву.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "ainura",
   "t": "А теперь убираю за конём.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "Быстро наведи в отеле порядок!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Quickly restore order in the hotel!' Eleonora colors one loaded choice in earnest: \"poryadok\" means \"order\", and it carries the main weight of what Eleonora is saying.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "Иначе я тебя отсюда вышвырну.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Otherwise I will throw you out of here.' Eleonora centers one practical element with Mikhail: \"vyshvyrnu\" means \"I will throw out\" (from \"vyshvyrnut\"), giving the line its exact edge.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "А вы двое слушайте меня.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'And you two listen to me.' Eleonora counters bluntly on the spot, shifting the whole mood of the room in a single beat.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "Неделю работаете совсем без зарплаты.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'You will work a week with no salary at all.' Eleonora uses this vivid detail toward Mikhail: \"rabotayete\" means \"work\" (from \"rabotat\"), giving the line its exact edge.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "И две недели без выходных.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'And two weeks without days off.' Eleonora chimes in at once without holding back, without trying to dress up how she really feels.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "Всё, быстро пошли вон отсюда!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'That is it, get out of here quickly!' Eleonora pushes back honestly to settle things, to clear the air between them once and for all.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "mikhail",
   "t": "Нет, это я не вам.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'No, I did not mean that for you.' Mikhail continues decisively without holding back, leaving no doubt about where he stands.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "mikhail",
   "t": "Да, я срочно продаю пони.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Yes, I am urgently selling a pony.' Mikhail continues lightly to be clear, watching Eleonora's face to see how the news lands.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "mikhail",
   "t": "Ещё как продаю, жду вас.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I sure am selling it, I am waiting for you.' Mikhail counters lightly facing Ainura, saying out loud what both of them already know.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "Айнура, быстро уберите всё здесь.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Ainura, quickly clean everything up here.' Eleonora uses this vivid element for Mikhail: \"uberite\" means \"take away, remove\" (from \"ubrat\"), giving the line its exact edge.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "ainura",
   "t": "Я приехала работать в Москву.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I came to work in Moscow.' Ainura speaks up honestly with a nod, shifting the whole mood of the room in a single beat.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "ainura",
   "t": "А теперь убираю за конём.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
